>I'll make this quick:
> 1) What do the statues do?

	Occasionally one will actually be a monster posing as a statue.  You
might smash one with a pick-axe to see if there's anything inside.  Usually,
all you'll get is rock, but somtimes not.

> 2) When you start a new game do the magic
>    items always have the same name?
>    Ex: Is a bubbly potion always the same?

	Usually not.  Certain items, like potions of water and some types of
armor, do retain their name between games.  Most of them don't.

> 3) I'll take any other helpful advice.  My 
>    characters rarely make it even down to the 
>    6th or 7th level.

	Ok...  Don't use an item unless 1) you're certain it's not cursed or
2) it doesn't really matter whether it's cursed or not.  One good test to
discover whether an item is cursed or not is to leave it on the floor and let
your pet step on it or pick it up.  Pets will usually not touch anything
cursed.

	When you get hungry, eat some monster corpses.  Don't keep them around
very long, though, unless you have some way to keep them from spoiling.  Some
corpses will convey certain abilities to you.

